      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Even though knitting machines seem mysterious, don't get overwhelmed!<br>\nYour journey to master your machine starts with de-mystifying the mechanics of our machines. <br>Learn to think of your machine as a tool - YOU are the boss! <i class=\"fa fa-smile-o aria-hidden=\"true\"></i><br><ul>\n<li>Basics</li>\n<li>Under the hood</li>\n<li>Terminology</li>\n</ul>\n<br\n<div class='text-center'>\n<a href=\"/downloads/beginner_worksheets.pdf\" class=\"kbm-btn kbm-btn-primary\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Print all pages of the Course Worksheets </a>\n</div>",
              "legacyComponentId": 4442,
              "order": 1,
              "layoutRole": "textVideoLeft"
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "178357401",
              "title": null,
              "legacyComponentId": 4441,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Your machine",
          "slug": "your-machine",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 1078,
            "blockType": "VimeoID"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "No matter what machine you have, the secret to stitch patterning (and other techniques) is to understand needle positions.<br><ul>\n<li> <a href=\"/glossary/out-of-work-position\" class=\"glossary-link\">Out of Work Position</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/glossary/working-position\" class=\"glossary-link\">Working Position</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/glossary/middle-position\" class=\"glossary-link\">Middle Position</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/glossary/holding-position\" class=\"glossary-link\">Holding Position</a></li>\n</ul>",
              "legacyComponentId": 4443,
