          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 1,
            "blockType": "HTML",
            "editorLayout": "textVideo"
          },
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<p>\nOne of the first questions new machine knitters ask is, \"What yarn can I use?\"\n</p>\n\n<p>\nIn this lesson, you'll learn:\n</p>\n\n<ul>\n    <li>Whether you need yarn on cones</li>\n    <li>How machine gauge affects your yarn choices</li>\n    <li>What needle pitch means</li>\n    <li>Why full needle rib requires a finer yarn</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>\nWatch the video first, then use the notes below as a handy reference whenever you're choosing yarn for your machine.\n</p>",
