    {
      "title": "Cast On Methods",
      "slug": "cast-on-methods",
      "displayOrder": 4,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 227,
        "lessonOrder": 4
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<h3>What Cast on to Use? Try these and judge for yourself</h3>\nAs with all things machine knitting, there are many, many ways of casting on your knitting.<div><br>When we first start knitting we are anxious to get stitches on the machine and get knitting. But we soon find that there may be better methods to cast on.</div>\n<div><br><b>Please don't get stuck in a rut and use the same cast on over and over.</b> Take time to LEARN and PRACTICE different methods.&nbsp;</div>\n<div>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Some are fast (but not good for the hem of a sweater).</li>\n        <li>Others are a more time consuming (but beautiful).</li>\n        <li>Some are stretchy enough for socks, others not so much.\n        </li>\n    </ul>On your machine knitting journey, it's up to you to discover the perfect cast on for your specific project.\n</div>\n<div><br><br>\n    <div><br><br>\n        <a href=\"/downloads/cast_on_exercises1.pdf\" class=\"kbm-btn kbm-btn-primary\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n            Print Cast On Worksheets\n        </a>\n</div></div>",
              "legacyComponentId": 4448,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "178357365",
              "title": "Explore an Open Cast On",
              "legacyComponentId": 2956,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "What Cast on to Use?",
          "slug": "open-cast-on",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 1081,
            "blockType": "VimeoID"
          }
        },
        {
          "title": "Open Cast On",
          "slug": "content-1782556698341",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3300,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          },
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Begin your knitting, leaving open stitches to be picked up later. Often worked with the <a href=\"/glossary/scrap-and-ravel-cast-on\" class=\"glossary-link\">Scrap and Ravel Cast On</a> method\n\n\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 8492,
              "order": 3,
              "layoutRole": "textVideoLeft"
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "178357365",
              "title": null,
              "legacyComponentId": 8493,
              "order": 4
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Closed Cast On",
          "slug": "three-videos-1782550753014",
          "order": 3,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3299,
            "blockType": "HTML",
            "editorLayout": "threeVideosWithText"
          },
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<p>\nWith a closed cast on, the starting stitches are secure. Here are a few methods for you to try.</p>\n<p>\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/33/Dont_skip.gif\"></p>\n\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 8484,
              "order": 5,
              "layoutRole": "threeVideosIntro"
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "178357361",
              "title": "Fast 'n Easy",
              "legacyComponentId": 8485,
              "order": 7,
              "layoutRole": "threeVideosVideo1"
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<ul>\n<li>Super Fast Closed Cast On</li>\n<li>Weaving Cast On</li>\n<li>E-Wrap Cast On</li>\n</ul><br><br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 8486,
              "order": 6,
              "layoutRole": "threeVideosCaption1"
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "317801328",
              "title": "Scrap on (Scrap and Ravel)",
              "legacyComponentId": 8487,
              "order": 9,
              "layoutRole": "threeVideosVideo2"
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\nThe technique of scrapping on is essential for you to learn.<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Protect delicate fibers and edges from a cast on comb</li>\n<li>Use as an open cast on for hems</li>\n<li>Make it easier to cast on using more complicated methods</li>\n</ul><br><br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 8488,
              "order": 8,
              "layoutRole": "threeVideosCaption2"
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "178357352",
              "title": "Better for Garment Edges",
              "legacyComponentId": 8489,
              "order": 11,
              "layoutRole": "threeVideosVideo3"
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<ul>\n<li>Double E-wrap</li>\n<li>Long Tail Cast On</li>\n<li>Chain Cast On</li>\n</ul>",
              "legacyComponentId": 8490,
              "order": 10,
              "layoutRole": "threeVideosCaption3"
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<img class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/33/Dont_skip.gif\">",
              "legacyComponentId": 8491,
              "order": 12,
              "layoutRole": "threeVideosOutro"
            }
          ]
