    {
      "title": "Finishing",
      "slug": "finishing",
      "displayOrder": 14,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 239,
        "lessonOrder": 14
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Just like in hand knitting, blocking techniques are a personal preference.<br>\n\n<b>Don't skip this topic.</b><br>  Blocking your knitting can mean the difference between \"home made\" and \"hand made\".<br>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Steaming</li>\n<li>Wet Blocking</li>\n<li>Wires</li>\n<li>Fibers</li>\n</ul>",
              "legacyComponentId": 4478,
              "order": 1,
              "layoutRole": "textVideoLeft"
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "178356993",
              "title": "Blocking: The finishing touch",
              "legacyComponentId": 2978,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Blocking",
          "slug": "blocking",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 1092,
            "blockType": "VimeoID"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Hopefully you've knit a bunch of swatches in this course. <b> Use these swatches to practice seaming.</b> <br>Never thought of seaming on the machine?  This is similar to using an expensive linker.  Give it a try!<br><br>Do your mattress stitch skills need work?  Practice now!<br><hr>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Seam on the Machine</li>\n<li>Mattress Stitch</li>\n<li>Tips for Perfection</li>\n</ul>",
              "legacyComponentId": 4480,
              "order": 1,
              "layoutRole": "textVideoLeft"
            },
